<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!-- No GeneratePackageOnBuild: it conflicts with `dotnet pack` on a multi-targeted Razor class
         library (NU5026/NU5019 from clean) and the documented publish uses `dotnet pack -o ./nupkg`
         then `nuget push nupkg/...`, which never reads the bin/Release package anyway. -->
    <Title>Blazor Controls</Title>
    <PackageId>WssBlazorControls</PackageId>
	  <AssemblyVersion>10.8.5</AssemblyVersion>
	  <FileVersion>$(AssemblyVersion)</FileVersion>
	  <Version>$(AssemblyVersion)</Version>

    <!-- Build hygiene: the changelog promises 0 warnings — enforce it. CS1591 excepted: the public
         surface is heavily XML-documented but not exhaustively, and missing-comment noise would
         drown real warnings. -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- Ship the XML docs so consumers get IntelliSense from the package. -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

    <!-- Debuggability + reproducibility: SourceLink is built into the .NET 8+ SDK; publish the
         repo URL, ship a .snupkg symbol package, and make CI builds deterministic. -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- Catches binary/source breaking changes against the previous published version at pack time. -->
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>

    <!-- Trimming / WASM AOT support. IsAotCompatible turns on IsTrimmable (the assembly-level
         [AssemblyMetadata("IsTrimmable","True")] that lets a consumer's trimmed publish actually trim
         this library) plus the trim/AOT/single-file Roslyn analyzers. With TreatWarningsAsErrors
         above, any new IL2xxx/IL3xxx regression fails the build. The reflection the library does
         (attribute reads via Field expressions, enum member lookups) is annotated or provably
         rooted — see EnumHelpers/FieldValidationDisplay for the reasoning. -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>

    <!-- Package Metadata -->
    <PackageDescription>A comprehensive library of form controls for Blazor applications, providing consistent, feature-rich input components with built-in validation, accessibility support, and flexible styling options.</PackageDescription>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <!-- SPDX expression (was PackageLicenseFile) so NuGet.org indexes/filters the license properly. -->
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>blazor;controls;forms;validation;accessibility;ui;components;webassembly;server</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
10.8.3 -- an additive, non-breaking release: two new form-level helpers, focus on every control, two new field parameters, a two-way-bindable EditRadioEnum "Other" field, and two attribute-handling contracts widened to cover every control that can use them.

NEW
- FormAutoSave: one component replacing per-field @bind-Value:after wiring for a whole form. Subscribes once to the EditContext, debounces changes (DebounceMilliseconds, default 500ms trailing) into one OnSave call carrying the changed fields. SaveWhenInvalid/Concurrency/ShouldSave/TimeProvider round out the configuration. OnSaveFailed hands back the fields a failed save was carrying -- they return to the front of the pending set and retry on the next flush instead of being lost; unwired, the exception re-dispatches for an ErrorBoundary.
- FormDefaults.FocusFirstField (bool?, default off): focuses a form's first rendered field once, after the scope's first render -- the form-level counterpart to the new FocusOnFirstRender below. Skips disabled/readonly/hidden fields, yields to an explicit FocusOnFirstRender on a specific control, retries up to 10 render batches for async-loaded forms, and needs no IJSRuntime registration to safely no-op.
- Public FocusAsync() and FocusOnFirstRender (bool, default false) on every Edit* control -- programmatic and declarative focus of whichever element a Tab into the control would land on. Never focuses a disabled/read-only/hidden control. Named FocusOnFirstRender, not AutoFocus, so a native autofocus attribute still splats through untouched.
- Suggestions (IEnumerable&lt;string&gt;?) on EditString/EditNumber: renders an open-vocabulary &lt;datalist&gt; hint, distinct from a Select control's closed vocabulary.
- LabelContent (RenderFragment?) on every control: rich-markup label content (icon plus text, etc.) in place of a plain Label string.
- EditRadioEnum&lt;TEnum&gt;: bind the "Other" free-text box two-way with @bind-OtherValue -- gives it a real FieldIdentifier, EditContext registration, and validation-summary participation.

CHANGED
- Event-handler chaining: a splatted onclick/onkeydown/onmousedown on EditRange, both date pickers, Modal/Drawer, and Select now chains with the control's own same-named handler instead of one discarding the other.
- The null-attribute-erasure fix (a splatted attribute surviving when the control has no opinion on it) now covers EditTextArea, EditDateNative, the EditSelect family, EditBool, and EditRange -- previously only EditString/EditNumber had it.

FIXED
- Every control's read-only rendered value now carries aria-describedby (description/tooltip/error text), previously reachable only in edit mode.
- EditCheckedEnumList/EditCheckedStringList's read-only fieldset and EditColor's read-only row are now correctly nameable to assistive tech.
- ToastQueue: an intermittent ObjectDisposedException race in Pause/Resume/Remove/Clear.
- FormDefaults no longer requires an IJSRuntime registration, fixing a crash under HtmlRenderer/out-of-band rendering (email templates, PDF export).
- AttributeSplat.RestExcept: a case-variant withheld attribute (e.g. aria-Label) is now actually removed instead of leaking a duplicate.

Full changelog: https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls#changelog
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>dcblakesley</Authors>
    <Company>WSS</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 WssBlazorControls</Copyright>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Include README and the package icon (license is declared via PackageLicenseExpression) -->
    <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
